# =============================================================================
# Sanjit-Majumdar Portfolio / .env.example
# =============================================================================
#
# This file is the SINGLE place where env-var requirements are documented
# for the sanjit-portfolio code repo. Copy it to `.env` for local development
# (gitignored) and populate the variables you need. For Vercel deployments,
# set each var under Project Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# SECURITY: `.env` is in `.gitignore` and must NEVER be committed. The
# `.env.example` itself IS tracked — keep it free of real secrets.
#
# Story 2-4 added the first set of variables (the content-repo clone). Future
# stories will append their own blocks below, ordered by story number.
#

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Story 2-4: shallow-clone of `sanjit-content` at build time
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# GIT_TOKEN: a GitHub fine-grained PAT with `contents:read` on the
# `sanjit-content` repo. The clone script (`scripts/clone-content.mts`)
# injects this into the clone URL when present. When absent, falls back to the
# public HTTPS URL form (works if the repo is public OR if the local user has
# a git credential helper configured for github.com).
#
# Vercel: add as a Secret environment variable on the production + preview
# environments. Mark it `Sensitive` so Vercel scrubs it from build logs.
#
# Local dev: copy this file to `.env`, populate `GIT_TOKEN=ghp_xxx`, then run
# the dev server (no need for Vercel secrets in `.env`).
#
# GIT_TOKEN=

# Override the source URL when the content repo is mirrored elsewhere
# (e.g., a fork used for testing). Defaults to
# `https://github.com/sanjit-majumdar/sanjit-content.git`.
# CONTENT_REPO_URL=

# When set to `1`, the clone step is skipped entirely and the reader runs
# against whatever is already in `content/` (useful for offline development or
# for testing pre-populated fixtures via `cp -r sanjit-content/content/* content/`).
# SKIP_CLONE=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Story 2-5: `POST /api/revalidate` edge handler
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# REVALIDATE_SECRET: a 32-byte hex string shared with the `sanjit-content`
# repo's GitHub Actions secret of the same name. The `sanjit-content` workflow
# (`sanjit-content/.github/workflows/revalidate.yml`) sends every webhook as
# `Authorization: Bearer $REVALIDATE_SECRET`; this handler verifies the token
# via constant-time compare (`crypto.subtle.timingSafeEqual`) before calling
# `revalidateTag(tag, 'max')`. Binds AD-1 (single read path) + NFR-S (no
# unauthorized revalidate).
#
# Generate the value once via:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Set both sides (rotation procedure in sanjit-content/docs/two-repo-contract.md
# §2 — change the value on Vercel first, then update the Actions secret; if
# the workflow's secret is updated first, in-flight webhooks will see 401s).
#
# Vercel: add as a Sensitive Secret environment variable on production +
# preview. Local dev: copy this file to `.env`, populate the same value.
#
# REVALIDATE_SECRET=
